## Structural self-audit

1. **Duplicate Event IDs:** PASS — 180 Events, 180 unique IDs.
2. **`null` Conditions:** PASS — 0 null condition fields.
3. **Queued Immediate IDs exist:** PASS — 135 queue edges; every target exists and is `kind: immediate`.
4. **Immediate cycles:** PASS — 0 cycles.
5. **Orphan Immediate Events:** PASS — 0; all 135 Immediate Events have an incoming queue edge.
6. **Specialized descendants without eligibility:** PASS — 0.
7. **Specialized Major roots without mini-arc:** PASS — 0; every specialized Major root has branch-specific Immediate continuation.
8. **Route-local fallback coverage:** PASS — Layer 1 has exactly one generic fallback; every previous-layer node is covered by exactly one next-layer fallback parent set.
9. **Broad crossings stealing more-specific routes:** PASS — specificity metadata is unchanged. `pirate_fishman_underkeel` remains priority 30 where it can overlap broader routes; the deliberate higher-specificity Layer-5 crossings remain ordered rather than weighted.
10. **Parent appearing despite incompatible current state:** PASS — every canonical parent placeholder resolves only from a root with matching current `originParentPresent` gating; Immediate descendants inherit those verified roots. Orphan/absent-parent routes do not materialize a parent.
11. **All descendant roots represented by routing scenarios:** PASS — all 40 descendant Major roots have exactly one declarative scenario; every scenario retains a complete prior Major History chain with structurally valid parent descent.
12. **Every Layer-5 leaf has a persistent reward:** PASS — 33/33 terminal leaves grant one of the five mandatory inheritance Items.
13. **FR/EN visible copy complete:** PASS — 0 missing FR/EN Event, Choice, or Outcome texts.
14. **No runtime-engine changes embedded:** PASS — no new Condition, Effect, GameState field, Flag, Scheduled handoff, or runtime primitive was introduced.

